{
  "$comment": [
    "EL CATÁLOGO DE LA FERIA — every ride, stall and booth as DATA.",
    "",
    "The world says WHERE a thing stands (churchill/world/content.py ->",
    "manifest.attractions); this says WHAT IT LOOKS LIKE. They are separate on",
    "purpose: the art is the part a person will want to change, and changing it",
    "should not mean editing a render function. The engine and the world editor",
    "read this file the same way they read src/ui/themeTokens.json — a registry",
    "they can build a form from and write back.",
    "",
    "A kind is a list of PARTS drawn from the ride's centre outward, in order,",
    "in the ride's own frame. Lengths are fractions of the ride's radius `r`",
    "unless the field name ends in Px. Every part may carry one animation:",
    "  spin:  turns/second (negative reverses)",
    "  swing: { amp: radians, speed: Hz }  — a pendulum about the centre",
    "  bob:   { amp: px, speed: Hz }       — up and down the screen",
    "",
    "Shapes: disc, ring, spokes, arms, cabins, box, awning, mast, pendulum,",
    "boat, dish, facade, track, bulbs, counter, sign.",
    "",
    "The roster is the one that actually comes to a Costa Rican turno — Zapote,",
    "Palmares, the Carnaval de Puntarenas — not a generic funfair."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "$schema": "Every ride is `{ name, note, parts: [...] }`. A part names a `shape` from the engine's finite vocabulary (`SHAPES` in src/render/c2d/attractions.js) and carries that shape's own fields; `r`/`spread`/`drop` are FRACTIONS of the ride's radius, `*Px` fields are absolute pixels. A part may carry ONE animation: `spin` (turns/s), `swing`, `bob` or `pump` — the same four verbs `src/assets/effects.json` documents for a vehicle part, because they are one vocabulary and not two.",
  "$gate": "tests/test_feria.py: every shape a ride names must be implemented, or the ride silently loses a piece — `drawAttraction` warns once to the console and carries on, which is correct at runtime and invisible in review. It also lists the shapes the engine implements that NO ride uses: art with nothing to select it is drift too, the lesson SignKind taught.",
  "$defaults": {
    "$note": "LOS VALORES POR OMISIÓN DEL MOTOR — lo que dibuja un verbo cuando la receta de un juego NO trae ese campo. Distinto del resto de las paletas del juego, y vale decir por qué: acá los juegos YA eran data desde que existe el campo ferial, y esto es la otra mitad, la que decide cómo se ve una pieza que nadie especificó. Antes estaban escritos como `p.fill || \"#dfe5ec\"` adentro de cada verbo, así que se podía cambiar el color de una rueda pero no el gris de la que se te olvidó pintar.",
    "disc": "#dfe5ec",
    "ring": "#dfe5ec",
    "spokes": "#b6bdc7",
    "arms": "#c7ccd3",
    "box": "#3b4250",
    "legs": "#8d949e",
    "mast": "#9aa3ae",
    "pendulumArm": "#c7ccd3",
    "pendulumCab": "#e85d75",
    "dish": "#2f3a4a",
    "dishRim": "#e0483f",
    "boat": "#8a5a35",
    "boatTrim": "#f3c969",
    "track": "#6a7280",
    "facade": "#3a2a4a",
    "facadeTrim": "#6b2f8f",
    "facadeDoor": "#0d0a12",
    "counter": "#b8875a",
    "counterTop": "#f6e7c8",
    "tarpEave": "#0e2258",
    "tarpRidge": "#2f6fc0",
    "tarpFill": "#17357f",
    "frame": "#e8ecef",
    "zinc": "#3a3b42",
    "zincRib": "#4d4f58",
    "zincEdge": "#24252a",
    "bannerGround": "#2b1b4d",
    "bannerInk": "#ffd400",
    "bannerAccent": "#c8102e",
    "neon": "#7dff5a",
    "goods": [
      "#e8c07a"
    ],
    "speaker": "#1d1826",
    "speakerCone": "#5a5170",
    "signFg": "#fff",
    "signBg": "#b3243b",
    "fallback": "#dfe5ec",
    "fallbackNote": "el gris de `pick()` cuando una paleta viene vacía."
  },
  "$chrome": {
    "$note": "Lo que NO es de un juego en particular: las guirnaldas entre las hileras de comida y la sombra que cada atracción tira. El tablado y sus luces se describen en materials.json.",
    "banderines": "rgba(240,244,248,0.7)",
    "bannerSeam": "rgba(255,255,255,0.18)",
    "awningShadow": "rgba(0,0,0,0.12)",
    "rideShadow": "rgba(0,0,0,0.16)",
    "stageShadow": "rgba(0,0,0,0.3)",
    "$speedNote": "LAS VELOCIDADES SON VUELTAS POR SEGUNDO (`t*spin*TAU`), no un número de gusto. Estaban 2–4 veces de más: la tómbola a 0.6 son 36 rpm y el carrusel a 0.18 son 11, cuando un carrusel de verdad hace 4–5 y una rueda 1–1,5. Un turno que gira demasiado rápido no se lee como una feria, se lee como un error. Referencias: rueda 1–1,5 rpm · carrusel 4–5 · sillas voladoras 8–10 · pulpo 6–8 · tagada 8–12.",
    "_groundNote": "EL SUELO ES UN TABLADO ELEVADO. Su receta vive en `materials.json -> feria.deck`; este catálogo sólo dibuja lo que se para encima."
  },
